Open the AWS Management Console.
Navigate to Route 53 → Hosted zones.
Select the hosted zone for aluru.site (or create a new hosted zone if it doesn’t exist).
Step 13.2: Create a Record Set

Click Create record.
Fill in the details:
Press enter or click to view image in full size

3. Click Create records.

Step 13.3: Verify DNS Resolution

Wait a few minutes for DNS propagation.
Test the DNS from your terminal or browser:
nslookup foodops.aluru.site
3. You should see your LoadBalancer’s IP or DNS returned.

Step 13.4: Access Your FoodOps Clone

Open your browser and navigate to:

http://FoodOps.aluru.site
Your Hotstar clone should load successfully, deployed via ArgoCD with full GitOps CI/CD automation.

